73
00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:45.570
These friends can take unlimited papers and spend them on making the politician win.

74
00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:53.340
This isn't bribery because you called it something else. (This is part of the six hundred and fifty million dollar lobbying

75
00:08:53.340 --> 00:09:02.740
budget.). Step 5: Give Papers You Get Back From The Government Back to the Rich Humans (Forever) Your treaty passes, redirecting

76
00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:09.580
twenty-seven point two billion dollars in papers annually. Eighty percent funds clinical trials (the point).

77
00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:13.480
Ten percent goes to a fund that rewards politicians who voted yes.

78
00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:18.060
Ten percent goes back to the rich humans as returns, forever.

79
00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:24.640
This is a good deal because forever is a long time. Unless you die from preventable diseases.

80
00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.340
Which you're fixing, so it works out. Why Your Leaders Aren't the Problem.

81
00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:37.220
With over two billion humans suffering from disease, you'd have to be a complete psychopath to make the conscious decision

82
00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:41.960
to spend six hundred and four times more on weapons than on helping them.

83
00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:48.000
But your leaders aren't monsters. They're just operating in a system that rewards the wrong things.

84
00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:55.200
Your civilization's incentive structure is the psychopath: Weapons manufacturers give politicians papers.

85
00:09:55.660 --> 00:10:02.380
Politicians use the papers to get people to vote for them. Voting for them gives them the power to give more papers to weapons

86
00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:06.400
manufacturers. Weapons manufacturers give them more papers.

87
00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:13.930
It's circular, like a dog chasing its tail, except the dog is democracy and the tail is made of money and corpses.

88
00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:18.780
No individual human in this loop is evil. The loop is evil.

89
00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:26.240
Every politician in it is making the locally rational choice: take the papers or lose your job to someone who will.

90
00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:31.440
It's a machine that converts good intentions into missiles, and it runs automatically.

91
00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:39.110
There's literally no voting your way out of this. It doesn't matter which political party is in power.

92
00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:46.340
Your "red team" and "blue team" argue about everything except the loop, because they're both inside it.

93
00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:52.120
They are all slaves to the same incentive structure, wearing different colored ties.

94
00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:56.980
Switching parties is like changing the wallpaper in a burning building.

95
00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:03.800
This manual doesn't ask politicians to become better people (that's clearly out of the question).

96
00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:09.120
It builds a better loop. You give them MORE papers to do the OPPOSITE thing.

97
00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:17.340
Same dog, same tail, but now the tail is made of cured diseases and the dog gets reelected for chasing it.

98
00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:27.840
Humanity's Death Wish. What's most endearing about your species is it KNOWS it's being illogical: You have movies about

99
00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:35.600
how wars are bad (which you watch between wars). You have books about peace (that you tax to buy bombs).

100
00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:41.070
You give prizes to people who promote peace (funded by weapons manufacturers).

101
00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:45.680
You have a "Department of Defense" (that mainly just attacks people).

102
00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:54.120
You have a "Department of Health" (that apparently makes coronaviruses and has not yet produced any observable health).

103
00:11:54.800 --> 00:12:02.820
It's like humanity is playing a game where the objective is to lose, but it is trying to lose as elaborately as possible.

104
00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:09.560
But I digress. That's an Earth word I learned. It means continuing after you should have stopped.

105
00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:16.080
Like your military spending. The Problem. The Daily Deletion Event.

106
00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:25.320
One hundred and fifty thousand humans permanently stop every twenty-four hours from diseases that are basically just bugs

107
00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:34.980
in your meat software. That's one Holocaust every forty days, except with fewer Nazis and more insurance paperwork (though

108
00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:40.940
some would argue the paperwork is worse; at least the Nazis were straightforward about the killing part).

109
00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:51.800
That's also fifty nine-elevens every single day, except nobody invades anyone about it because diseases don't have oil.

110
00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:57.630
Your body is quietly falling apart. Your cells are forgetting how to cell properly.

111
00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:02.700
Your cancer cells are multiplying RIGHT NOW. Your telomeres are shortening.

112
00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:07.960
You are literally dissolving. You're a meat robot with worn-out parts.

113
00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:12.640
Every one of these failures is a solvable engineering problem.

114
00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:16.720
You'd think humans would prioritize solving these problems.

115
00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:23.600
You'd be adorable for thinking that. The Unexplored Therapeutic Frontier.

116
00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:28.860
Ninety-five percent of your diseases have zero F.D.A.-approved treatments.

117
00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:38.160
This means Food and Drug Administration has not administered drugs for ninety-five percent of food-and-drug-related problems.

118
00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:43.100
Only fifteen diseases get their first effective treatment each year.

119
00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:48.180
Six thousand six hundred and fifty diseases are still waiting.

120
00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:56.420
There are nine thousand five hundred known safe compounds, and ninety-nine point seven percent of their potential uses have

121
00:13:56.420 --> 00:14:03.700
never been tested. At the current discovery rate, finding treatments for all of them will take about four hundred and forty-three

122
00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:09.620
years. Everyone currently alive will be dead by then. The Cost of War.

123
00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:19.140
Humans spend two point seven two trillion dollars every year on stuff designed specifically to make humans stop being alive:

124
00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:26.640
Thirteen thousand nuclear warheads (enough to end civilization thirteen times, just in case the first twelve apocalypses

125
00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:32.390
don't take). A.I. murder-bots. Invisible jets that cost more than hospitals.

126
00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:38.860
Space Force (to fight the zero aliens attacking you). And some kind of earthquake machine (probably).

127
00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:46.180
Government spending on clinical trials: six hundred and four times less than military spending.

128
00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:50.520
Your chance of dying from terrorism: one in thirty million.

129
00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:58.840
Your chance of dying from disease: one hundred percent. If cancer had oil reserves, you would have cured it by two thousand

130
00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:06.900
and three. Instead, you spent the repair money on murder tubes that cost more than countries and submarines that hide underwater,

131
00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:11.460
as if that's somehow useful when you live on land. The F.D.A.

132
00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:20.740
is Unsafe and Ineffective. Even the money you DO spend on medicine is mostly wasted, because the system that approves treatments

133
00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:29.140
is a smoke detector that works by mail. Vioxx killed an estimated thirty-eight thousand to fifty-five thousand people from

134
00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:35.400
heart attacks. The F.D.A. approved it. When patients started dying, someone filled out a P.D.F.

135
00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:43.100
form. A P.D.F. Then they faxed it. (Yes, in the twenty-first century.) Then a human read it.

136
00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:48.960
Five years and tens of thousands of corpses later, someone noticed a pattern.

137
00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:58.060
This is your safety system. Your National Institutes of Health, the agency nominally responsible for finding cures, spends

138
00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:01.880
three point three percent of its budget on clinical trials.

139
00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:07.720
The other about ninety-seven percent goes to basic research, administration, and buildings.

140
00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:12.400
It's like a fire department that spends three percent of its budget on water.

141
00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:20.220
Then there's an eight point two years delay between proving a drug is safe and letting dying humans take it.

142
00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:25.200
The drug passed the safety test. Everyone agrees it won't kill you.

143
00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:32.660
But you still can't have it because a committee needs to spend eight point two years making sure it works well enough.

144
00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:40.180
You'd volunteer for the trials that would answer that question faster, but so would one point zero eight billion other patients,

145
00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:47.900
and the current system has one point nine million slots. That's a participation rate of zero point zero six percent.

146
00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:54.960
It's like a lifeguard who confirms the life preserver floats, then locks it in a cabinet for years to study its buoyancy

147
00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:59.400
profile while a billion people drown in line for the two available life jackets.

148
00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:08.720
Your regulatory system can make two mistakes: approve a bad drug (Type one error), or block a good drug (Type two error).

149
00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:13.960
Your F.D.A. is terrified of the first mistake and completely ignores the second.

150
00:17:14.859 --> 00:17:23.200
I calculated the ratio: for every one person protected from a dangerous drug, three thousand and seventy people die waiting

151
00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:31.160
for a safe one that's locked in the approval cabinet. Even if you assume a Thalidomide-scale catastrophe happens during

152
00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:38.680
post-phase one efficacy testing every single year (even though it wouldn't because Phase one safety testing actually caught

153
00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:46.800
it anyway), the deaths from just the efficacy delay still outnumber the deaths from bad drugs by three thousand and seventy

154
00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:52.500
to one. Your safety system's main product is dead patients.

155
00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:59.420
The good news: You already know how to fix this. The bad news: It requires you to do something.

156
00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:06.220
The weird news: You'll get rich doing it. The Solution. A one percent Treaty.

157
00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:15.260
This is going to sound crazy. But you're going to use those papers to persuade the leader of every country on Earth to simultaneously

158
00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:19.540
redirect one percent of its military budget to clinical trials.

159
00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:29.380
That's it. That's the treaty. After the craziness objection, the second objection every human has: "But if we cut our military

160
00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:35.400
budget, our enemies will invade us!". Everyone cuts one percent at the same time.

161
00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:43.620
Your national security actually *increases*, because everyone has one percent fewer missiles pointed at them.

162
00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:51.720
And if you still feel like doing war, two point six nine trillion dollars is still enough to murder every man, woman, and

163
00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:55.380
child on Earth twenty times, which should be more than sufficient.

164
00:18:56.620 --> 00:19:01.540
"But humans would never agree to a treaty!" you say. You already have.

165
00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:06.980
Multiple times. You banned chemical weapons (nineteen ninety-three, one hundred and ninety-three countries).

166
00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:12.490
You banned biological weapons (nineteen seventy-five, one hundred and eighty-seven countries).

167
00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:17.240
You banned landmines (nineteen ninety-seven, one hundred and sixty-four countries).

168
00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:21.780
You've signed treaties banning weapons you actually like using.

169
00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:27.630
This one just asks you to buy one percent fewer of them. I've done this before.

170
00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:34.620
I've sent versions of this manual to eight hundred and forty-seven civilizations on eight hundred and forty-seven planets.

171
00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:45.680
Some listened. Some didn't. I kept the data. The civilizations that redirected resources from killing each other to keeping

172
00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:49.760
each other alive transcended war and disease. The ones that didn't extincted themselves.

173
00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.840
The difference was never intelligence, technology, or resources.

174
00:19:54.340 --> 00:20:00.880
The only variable was the percentage of the population that decided it sounded crazy without reading the next page.

175
00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:10.140
That is the same reflex that kept you from inventing antibiotics for two hundred thousand years while bread mold sat right

176
00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:18.840
there on your bread. And you have two other advantages, the internet and a new financial instrument designed specifically

177
00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:24.200
for harnessing the most powerful force in the universe: human greed.

178
00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:32.540
Your Decentralized F.D.A. On Wishonia, we built this with the funding from our version of the treaty, three thousand years

179
00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:37.920
ago. Every treatment is tracked in real time. Every outcome is published.

180
00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:46.100
Every patient can participate. We don't have a word for "unapproved medicine" because we don't have a bureaucracy that sits

181
00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:52.080
on safe treatments while people die. You'd call our system a decentralized F.D.A.

182
00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:58.600
Here's what yours would look like, adjusted for the fact that you require small pieces of paper before you'll do anything.

183
00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:07.900
Eighty percent of the twenty-seven point two billion dollars will go directly to subsidizing patient participation in pragmatic

184
00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:16.020
trials at nine hundred and twenty-nine dollars per patient instead of the usual forty-one thousand dollars.

185
00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:21.000
Patients will choose which trials to join; their subsidy will follow them.

186
00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:24.600
Treatment developers and providers will get paid for each participant.

187
00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:29.440
No grant committees deciding which diseases are fashionable this year.

188
00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:34.040
Pragmatic trials will integrate into the standard healthcare system.

189
00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:39.420
Real patients will participate instead of two hundred people hand-picked by pharmaceutical companies.

190
00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:49.380
The whole thing will use your new decentralized F.D.A. protocol, reducing trial costs by forty-four point one times and

191
00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:58.120
funding twenty-three point four million patients per year (versus the current one point nine million patients per year).

192
00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:03.140
Remember that billion patients drowning in line for two life jackets?

193
00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:08.900
